l history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  verbal consent was obtained  3 aspirates were performed using 23 and 25 gauge  needles without anesthesia and without complications  3 slides were stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Rapid Interpretation  Benign ductal epithelium     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to N P  Connie Roche by phone  at 5 o clock P M         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Ivan A Chebib MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 08       CLINICAL HISTORY    27 year old female with left breast area of pain and hardness x 1 year  US  left  upper outer region   no sonographic abnormality        SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 3 slides in ETOH and 3 air dried slides   Received 5cc s of clear colorless fluid  One SurePath slide made           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Positive.
