ng from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section laboratory is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a 1 3cm rubbery nodule on one edge obliterating the resection margin  inked and sectioned to reveal the nodule to be ill defined  bulging  tan brown and focally red  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in A  The rest of the mass is submitted in B  Some tissue is saved for E R  studies  The remaining non frozen tissue is submitted entirely in C E  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  suture at apex of axilla  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast  15 x 15 x 3 5cm  an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9cm skin ellipse  and 7 x 4 x 2 5cm axillary tail  The entire specimen weighs 415 grams  A 3cm recent incision with sutures is present centrally 3cm away from the closest skin margin  Beneath this is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 3cm cavity containing fresh blood clot  The cavity is partially surrounded by 0 5cm thick firm  indurated  white tan mass at the posterior surface  grossly 1cm away from the deepest resection margin  In addition  a 4 x 3 x 2cm area inferior and adjacent to the cavity is tan yellow  hemorrhagic and focally firm  The remaining parenchyma is mostly yellow  lobulated with focal rubbery  white areas  The nipple  which is 0 5cm superior to the incision  does not have a pigmented areola  and is unremarkable  The axillary lymph nodes are white tan  focally firm  the largest being 0 9cm  Section Code F  representative sections of firm areas surrounding the cavity G H   representative sections of the hemorrhagic areas around the cavity I   deepest resection margin J L   other deep resection margin