VED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm area of architectural distortion that was somewhat ill defined  ovoid and  irregular  hypoechoic  and without significant internal vascularity     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     3 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   4 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by palpation under the Amy Ly M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  Connie Roche RN was notified of the preliminary results by personal  communication at 3 30 pm           The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Amy Ly MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 07       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast DCIS  status post excision  New palpable lump with associated  tenderness near surgical site         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 3 slides in ETOH and 4 air dried slides     B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  name and  medical number   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a collodion bag  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID            Specimen  BREAS