Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 22 CLINICAL DATA  History of new density in inner medial aspect of right breast  Previous right breast biopsy revealed a benign lesion  On physical exam no discrete right breast mass evident  Dense fibrous tissue in upper quadrant of right breast  No supraclavicular  axillary  or cervical adenopathy  Status post colon carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED WITH FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND FOCUS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor measures 1 1cm in greatest diameter on the histologic sections and comes within 0 2cm of the nearest inked margin  Blood vessel invasion is not identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen recptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm red and yellow soft piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan firm lesion with irregular borders  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of the remainder are submitted in A through J  with A through D corresponding to the suspicious lesion  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unknown.
